From 25014d772a651c49d99c8f617116c7989a247369 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:40:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Matrix editor support (touchpad / auto mouse settings
 over VIA)

- matrix_pointing.c/.h: answer the Matrix editor on the VIA custom
  channel, keep the settings in the user EEPROM datablock and apply them
  (CPI, rotation / inversion, acceleration, scroll, auto mouse layer).
- digitizer_user.c: CPI comes from the saved setting (default 1600 as
  before); the Matrix transform runs after the existing smoothing.
- keymap.c: load the settings at startup (auto mouse layer defaults to
  _MOUSE as before) and track key presses for the post-typing delay.
- config.h: DYNAMIC_KEYMAP_LAYER_COUNT 5 so the _MOUSE layer (layer 4) is
  part of the VIA keymap; with the default of 4 every key on it reads as
  KC_NO, which disables the keyboard while the auto mouse layer is on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
